                        <hr size='1' width='100%' color='#000000'><a name="entry205"></a>

                        <span id='postcolor'>Okay after a few long hours of haxxoring away; fun feature added.<br><br>You know how those "other" places only list the min and max for a spell&#39;s damage or otherwise detrimental/beneficial effects? <br><br>Well, for spells that have "valid&#39; formula&#39;s (meaning my script can actually take the formula and calculate a result without errors), it&#39;ll show you all steps from minimum damage to maximum damage and level.<br><br>So, for example: The level 24 Magician spell "Shock of Spikes" does a minimum of &nbsp;158 damage at level 24, up to a maximum of 176 at level 30.<br><br>Suppose you&#39;re level 28? How much damage does it do then? Easy - scroll down the page, and look for a &#39;Spell Progression&#39; box. It&#39;ll list the "stat" affected and how much the effect is at a certain level. So, we can now see that at level 28, the Shock of Spikes spell does 170 points of HitPoint damage. <br><br>Fun huh? <br><br>It works for most spells too - even resist debuffs and buffs on a sliding scale <!--emo&:D--><img src="http://www.theoutwardeye.com/iB_html/non-cgi/emoticons/biggrin.gif" border="0" valign="absmiddle" alt=':D'><!--endemo--><br><br>(happay&#33<!--emo&;)--><img src="http://www.theoutwardeye.com/iB_html/non-cgi/emoticons/wink.gif" border="0" valign="absmiddle" alt=';)'><!--endemo-->  </span>

